    <string name="alert_until">Until %1$s</string>
    <string name="cloud_help">Cloud cover is the percentage of the sky covered by clouds. It does not measure rain probability.</string>
    <string name="snow_help">Snowfall is the forecast accumulation for the reported interval. Snow depth and the liquid-water equivalent are different measurements.</string>
    <string name="radiation_help">Solar radiation measures the incoming sunlight per square metre, in W/m². Clouds and the time of day affect this value.</string>
    <string name="cape_help">CAPE describes energy available for atmospheric convection, in J/kg. It is one indicator used to assess developing showers; it does not by itself predict a thunderstorm.</string>
    <string name="forecast_help">Values use the selected weather source and the local time of this location. Missing intervals are left blank.</string>
